  "title": "Kirat A NDE 6139",
  "date": "30-5-2009",
  "content": "It was 30th May 2009. I was being operated on for a hernia. As scheduled, I was shifted to the operating theater. Soon I was unconsciousness under the effect of anesthesia. The next thing I can remember, I was observing the operation from the ceiling. I had a comfortable 'rial view of the surgery. I could see my dad who was inside the operating theater. I could see the surgeon and the nurse standing to the left of me. Suddenly, I went up higher and felt extreme happiness and peace, which I had never ever experienced. It was divine. I suddenly started falling back in a deep dark tunnel. As I fell in the tunnel, a few past events of my life were visible to me and they went past me in a fraction of a second. Next thing I remember was waking up in the ward of the hospital. I always thought that it was a dream. Two years later, I was reading about NDEs on the internet and I found my experience similar to the experiences depicted there. Out of curiosity, I asked my dad about it. My dad is a psychiatrist and has been practicing since 23 years. He was present in the operating theater. He told me that I was gasping at one point during the operation and that the situation was grave. I was shocked to know this. But since then, I've had a tremendous transformation. I was a GOD-hater. Suddenly I've started reading a lot of spiritual literature. I feel happier and safe. I don't fear death anymore and never get depressed at the problems I face in life.",
